Z||000004||Raydar||04-09-2001||10:11 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>I wanna know how it sounds with a cat and resonator tips, no muffler.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  that'd be fun</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><B>THRUMMMMMMM!!!</B><BR>Been there. Done that. You can't carry on a conversation with the windows down. Kinda reminds me of the pressure wave that occurs when you remove the sunroof, leave the deflector off, and roll up the windows. It's NOT pleasant. I ended up having a bullet glasspack welded in, upstream from the split. It's better, but still loud enough to set off car alarms in the parking garage at work. (Security just <I>loves</I> me.)<BR>Of course, this is a 44 year old's point of view. Your mileage may vary.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||13
